# Technical Summary — Chicaffe

## 1. Functional Requirements (Agile & UI/UX)
* **FR-01.** The system must allow new users to register by providing their full name, email address, and password.
* **FR-02.** The system must validate that the email entered during registration is not already associated with an existing account.
* **FR-03.** The system must display a validation message for each required field left empty.
* **FR-04.** The system must authenticate users through Supabase Auth using email and password.
* **FR-05.** The system must redirect the user to the admin dashboard after a successful login.
* **FR-06.** The system must allow users to close their active session at any time.
* **FR-07.** After logout, the system must prevent access to protected pages without re-authentication.
* **FR-08.** The system must allow administrators to manage users, tables, products, and addresses.
* **FR-09.** The system must manage the order lifecycle (pending → in_progress → delivered → cancelled).
* **FR-10.** The system must automatically decrease product inventory when items are added to an order and restore it if an order is cancelled.
* **FR-11.** **(New)** The system must allow searching for users and products by name via a global search bar.
* **FR-12.** **(New)** The system must generate a daily sales report for administrative tracking.

---

## 2. Agile Requirements
* **AG-01.** The project must be organized into Sprints of fixed duration with defined goals.
* **AG-02.** Every User Story must follow the format: As a [user type], I want to [action], so that [benefit].
* **AG-03.** Every User Story must have acceptance criteria written in Gherkin format (Given / When / Then).
* **AG-04.** Every User Story must have an estimated Story Point value assigned.
* **AG-05.** All source code must be version-controlled with Git and hosted on GitHub.

---

## 3. UI/UX Requirements
* **UX-01.** The application must have a consistent visual identity across all sections: colors, typography, and logo.
* **UX-02.** All pages must be responsive and adapt correctly to desktop screen sizes.
* **UX-03.** Navigation between modules must be accessible from a persistent sidebar menu.
* **UX-04.** All destructive actions (delete, cancel) must display a confirmation dialog before executing.
* **UX-05.** Products with zero stock must be visually marked as "Out of stock".
* **UX-06.** **(New)** The system must provide a search input at the top of data tables for quick filtering.

---

## 4. Non-Functional Requirements
* **NFR-01.** All data listings must load in under 3 seconds under normal network conditions.
* **NFR-02.** Saving a new record must complete and reflect in the UI within 2 seconds.
* **NFR-03.** User passwords must never be stored in plain text; Supabase Auth must handle credential management.
* **NFR-04.** The system must be built exclusively with HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and Supabase.
* **NFR-05.** The system is designed and tested for modern Chromium-based browsers.
* **NFR-06.** **(New)** The system must detect loss of internet connection and notify the user immediately to prevent data loss.
* **NFR-07.** **(New)** The `unit_price` in `ORDER_DETAIL` must be historically preserved (frozen) at the time of the order.

---

## 5. Data Structure (Entity-Relationship Diagram)

```mermaid
erDiagram

    %% SECTION 1 — USERS & ADDRESSES
    USER ||--o{ ADDRESS : "has"
    USER ||--o{ ORDER : "places/manages"

    USER {
        int id_user PK
        varchar full_name
        varchar email
        varchar password_hash "managed by Supabase Auth"
        timestamp created_at
    }

    ADDRESS {
        int id_address PK
        int id_user FK
        varchar street
        varchar city
        varchar state
        varchar postal_code
    }

    %% SECTION 2 — TABLES & PRODUCTS
    TABLE {
        int id_table PK
        int table_number "UNIQUE"
        int capacity
    }

    PRODUCT {
        int id_product PK
        varchar name "UNIQUE"
        text description
        decimal price
    }

    %% SECTION 3 — ORDERS & DETAILS
    TABLE ||--o{ ORDER : "assigned to"
    ORDER ||--|{ ORDER_DETAIL : "contains"
    PRODUCT ||--o{ ORDER_DETAIL : "included in"

    ORDER {
        int id_order PK
        int id_user FK
        int id_table FK
        timestamp order_date
        enum status "pending | in_progress | delivered | cancelled"
        int created_by_admin FK "Audit tracking"
    }

    ORDER_DETAIL {
        int id_detail PK
        int id_order FK
        int id_product FK
        int quantity
        decimal unit_price "Price frozen at order time"
    }

    %% SECTION 4 — INVENTORY
    PRODUCT ||--o{ INVENTORY : "tracked in"

    INVENTORY {
        int id_movement PK
        int id_product FK
        enum movement_type "SALE | RESTOCK"
        int quantity
        timestamp movement_date
        text notes
    }
```

---

## 6. Expanded Product Backlog

### EP-06 · Reports & Analytics (New)

#### US-11 — Daily Sales Report
*As an* administrator,
*I want to* view the total sales for the current day,
*So that* I can perform a cash out without manual calculation errors.

*Priority:* Medium | *Story Points:* 3

> **Acceptance Criteria:**
> * **Given** the administrator is on the "Reports" section.
> * **When** they select the current date.
> * **Then** the system sums the total of all `ORDER_DETAIL` records linked to "delivered" orders for that day.

---

### EP-01 · User Authentication (Ampliación)

#### US-12 — Admin Password Recovery
*As an* administrator,
*I want to* request a password reset email,
*So that* I can regain access if I forget my credentials.

*Priority:* Low | *Story Points:* 3

